ts to promote Church unity, c) desire to live in harmony with other Christians. The learner is guided to:  brainstorm on the meaning of , unity of believers,  read John 15:1-10 and discuss how the metaphor of vine and its branches describes unity of believers,  create an artistic representation of the vine and branches,  dramatise the metaphor of the bride of Christ,  read 2 Corin, , the learner should be able to: a) describe the Lord’s supper and its meaning, b) interpret the events that took place on Mount Olives, c) compile the events in Luke 22:54-71, 23:1-56 and lessons learnt, d) identify witnesses to the risen Christ and the significance, e) relate how they respond to Christ’ sacrificial work on the cross, f) explain the ascension and the second coming of Christ, g) appreciate the sacrificial work of Christ on the cross. The learner is guided to:  share experiences','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','','kicd','active','https://kicd.ac.ke/','KICD Curriculum Designs','2024','2024','');
