nverts to Islam, c) appreciate the role played by earliest converts to the development of Islam. The learner is guided to: • mention the earliest converts in Islam (Khadija (R.a.) Ali (R.A.) and Abubakar (R.A.), in pairs/groups, and write them in their notebook, • read from reference material/course books on the story of (Khadija (R.a.) Ali (R.A.) and Abubakar (R.A.) and writ, , the learner should be able to: a) identify the pillars of prayers for validity of swalah, b) apply the pillars of swalah correctly in daily prayers, c) appreciate the need for observing the pillars of swalah by emulating the Sunnah of the Prophet (S.A.W.). The learner is guided to: • pick the pillars of swalah (niyyah, qiyam, takbiratul ihram, reciting al-Fatiha, rukuu, raising from rukuu, sujud, siting between the sujud, sitting while reciting the last tashahhud, tashahhud, prayers for Ibrahi','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','','kicd','active','https://kicd.ac.ke/','KICD Curriculum Designs','2024','2024','');
