ctly in oral and written contexts, c) use the modals could and would and the phrase how many...could/would in sentences correctly, d) judge the appropriateness of adverbs used in oral and written texts. The learner is guided to: • identify and list adverbs from a digital or print text collaboratively, • make sentences from a substitution table using the pattern how many...coul, , the learner should be able to: a) identify collective nouns and reflexive pronouns in texts, b) use collective nouns and reflexive pronouns in sentences correctly, c) adopt the use of collective and reflexive pronouns during communication. The learner is guided to: • identify reflexive pronouns and collective nouns from print and digital texts, • watch a video clip in which collective nouns and reflexive pronouns (myself, ourselves) have been used in sentences, • team up to pick out collective','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','','kicd','active','https://kicd.ac.ke/','KICD Curriculum Designs','2024','2024','');
