ills in Handball, c) execute dribbling in Handball for skill acquisition, d) execute jump shot in Handball for enjoyment, e) appreciate each other''s efforts in playing Handball game. The learner is guided to: • watch a virtual or observe a demonstration of passes, dribbling and shooting in Handball, • demonstrate the side, jump and flick passes in Handball, • practise the pass, , the learner should be able to: a) describe techniques used in storytelling, b) explain qualities of a good flipbook, c) compose a 3 to 5- minute story addressing an issue in society, d) create a flipbook animation for storytelling, e) perform a 3 to 5- minute story before an audience, f) realise storytelling as a means of communication. The learner is guided to: • watch live/recorded narration clips to discuss storytelling techniques (use of voice, use of body, use of songs, audience involveme','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','[]','','kicd','active','https://kicd.ac.ke/','KICD Curriculum Designs','2024','2024','');
